the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base n0009_invocation_arithmetic includes these resources:
    maths.

the functions are:
    the amount of the loan is *a number*.
    the rate of the loan is *a number*.
    the term of the loan is *a number*.
    the fee is *a number*.
    the pmt of *a value* and *a second value* and *a third value* is *a fourth value*.
    the monthly payment is *a number*.

the knowledge base n0009_invocation_arithmetic includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/0009-invocation-arithmetic.dmn".

the pmt of a value V and a value N and a value M is a value K if
    a number P = 1 + N / 12
    and an exponent E = 0 - M
    and the power of P to E is a result R
    and K = V * N / 12 / (1 - R).

rule monthly_payment_1 with provenance the model at decision MonthlyPayment:
the monthly payment is a number N if
    the pmt of the amount of the loan and the rate of the loan and the term of the loan is a value V
    and N = V + the fee.

